   "desc": "Part (b): a correct response says that choosing 3 objects from 9 is the same act as choosing which 6 to leave behind, so the two counts must agree -- equivalently, the two factorial expressions have the same denominator with its factors written in the other order. In the expansion this is the left-right symmetry of a row of Pascal's triangle. Full credit gives a reason of that kind; computing the second value and observing that it matches is a check, not an explanation, and earns partial credit only.",
